Q: Removing empty values from a list and assigning it to a new list A: <p>Please try as below</p>
<pre class="lang-yaml prettyprint-override"><code>  vars:
   list1: [ &quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;, &quot;&quot;, &quot;7&quot;, &quot;&quot; ]
   list2:  []

  tasks:
  - name: test
    set_fact:
     list2: &quot;{{list2  + [item]}}&quot;
    when: item != &quot;&quot;
    with_items:
     - &quot;{{list1}}&quot;

</code></pre>
<p>Output</p>
<pre><code>ok: [localhost] =&gt; {
    &quot;msg&quot;: [
        &quot;a&quot;,
        &quot;b&quot;,
        &quot;7&quot;
    ]
}
</code></pre>

Q: Check if a string is palindrome in C A: <p>You <code>pali</code> function tests if the first character of the string is equal to the last character and then invokes itself for a position of the second character of the string. Note however, it does not modify <em>the end of a string</em>, so the recursive invocation compares the second character again to the last one. Then you compare the third charcter to the last one... Finaly <code>pali</code> returns <code>1</code> if <em>all characters</em> are equal to the last one, that is if all are equal.</p>
<p>Try this (well, do not; see below):</p>
<pre><code>// incorrect code, kept for the comment consistency
int pali (char* texto)
{
   char* end;
   for(end = texto; *end != '\0'; end ++)
       ;

   for(--end; texto &lt; end; ++texto, --end) {
      if(* texto != * end)
          return 0;
   }
   return 1;
}
</code></pre>
<p><strong>EDIT</strong></p>
<p>The code above has been found incorrect. When the input string is empty we have <code>*texto == 0</code>, so the first <code>for</code> loop does nothing except setting <code>end = texto</code>. Then the second loop starts with <code>--end</code>, which shifts the <code>end</code> pointer <em>before</em> the string's first character (which in this case is a terminating NUL character).</p>
<p>And this – as user <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/users/2410359/chux">@chux</a> correctly pointed out in the comment (now deleted) – invokes Undefined Behavior.</p>
<p>Here is a fixed code</p>
<pre><code>int pali (char* texto)
{
   char* end = texto;
   while(* end != '\0')
       end ++;

   while(texto &lt; end) {
      if(* texto++ != * --end)
          return 0;
   }
   return 1;
}
</code></pre>
<p>The first loop seeks the end of the input string, same as in previous version. As a result, before the second loop the <code>end</code> pointer points at the string's terminator, so it is one character <em>past</em> the one to be compared. OTOH the <code>texto</code> points at the first character (if any), so it is at the right position. That's why <code>end</code> is decremented <em>before</em> fetching the character for comparison and <code>texto</code> is incremented <em>after</em> fetching the character.</p>
<p>The necessary condition is that the character fetched for comparison through <code>end</code> does not <em>precede</em> that fetched through <code>texto</code>, which requires <code>texto &lt; end</code> before decrementing <code>end</code>.<br />
This is guaranteed by the <code>while</code> loop condition.</p>

Q: What is the purpose of &quot;&amp;&amp;&quot; in a shell command? A: <pre><code>from flask import Flask, render_template, request, redirect, session
import random

app = Flask(__name__)
app.secret_key = &quot;secret_key&quot;

# Lưu tạm dữ liệu (demo)
users = {}
otp_store = {}

# Trang chủ
@app.route('/')
def home():
    return render_template(&quot;index.html&quot;)

# Trang đăng ký
@app.route('/register', methods=['GET', 'POST'])
def register():
    if request.method == 'POST':
        phone = request.form['phone']
        otp = str(random.randint(100000, 999999))
        otp_store[phone] = otp

        print(f&quot;Mã OTP cho {phone}: {otp}&quot;)  # Hiển thị OTP trong terminal

        return render_template(&quot;verify.html&quot;, phone=phone)

    return render_template(&quot;register.html&quot;)

# Xác nhận OTP
@app.route('/verify', methods=['POST'])
def verify():
    phone = request.form['phone']
    otp = request.form['otp']

    if otp_store.get(phone) == otp:
        users[phone] = True
        return &quot;Đăng ký thành công!&quot;
    else:
        return &quot;Sai OTP!&quot;

# Trang đăng nhập
@app.route('/login', methods=['GET', 'POST'])
def login():
    if request.method == 'POST':
        phone = request.form['phone']

        if phone in users:
            otp = str(random.randint(100000, 999999))
            otp_store[phone] = otp
            print(f&quot;OTP đăng nhập {phone}: {otp}&quot;)

            return render_template(&quot;verify_login.html&quot;, phone=phone)
        else:
            return &quot;Số chưa đăng ký!&quot;

    return render_template(&quot;login.html&quot;)

# Xác nhận OTP đăng nhập
@app.route('/verify_login', methods=['POST'])
def verify_login():
    phone = request.form['phone']
    otp = request.form['otp']

    if otp_store.get(phone) == otp:
        session['user'] = phone
        return f&quot;Đăng nhập thành công: {phone}&quot;
    else:
        return &quot;Sai OTP!&quot;

app.run(debug=True)
</code></pre>
